{%- comment -%}
  Clears the CHECKOUT VAT declaration whenever the buyer is back on the
  storefront.

  Render once in layout/theme.liquid, just before </body>:

    {% render 'vat-relief-reset' %}

  Why this exists: `_vat_relief_confirmed_at` is a cart attribute, so it
  survives the buyer leaving checkout. Without this, a buyer who ticks the
  declaration, goes back to the cart, and returns to checkout finds the box
  still ticked and the attestation already made — for a checkout visit they
  have not actually read. The declaration has to be made fresh each time they
  arrive at checkout, or it is not a declaration.

  Checkout is not rendered by the theme, so this can never fire while the buyer
  is IN checkout. It only runs on storefront pages, which is exactly where
  "they left checkout" is observable.

  Cost control: the POST only happens when there is something to clear. Liquid
  already knows the current value, so a normal page view with no confirmation
  outstanding makes no request at all.

  The `pageshow` handler covers the back button. A bfcache restore does not
  re-run inline scripts, so a buyer who ticks at checkout and then hits Back
  would otherwise return to a page whose script already ran, with the stale
  confirmation intact.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    var outstanding = {% if cart.attributes['_vat_relief_confirmed_at'] != blank %}true{% else %}false{% endif %};

    function clearConfirmation() {
      return fetch('/cart/update.js', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json'},
        // Shopify deletes an attribute set to the empty string.
        body: JSON.stringify({attributes: {_vat_relief_confirmed_at: ''}}),
      }).catch(function () {
        /* A failed clear leaves the stale confirmation in place. The buyer is
         * not blocked by that — worst case they are not asked to re-tick — so
         * it is not worth an error in front of them. */
      });
    }

    if (outstanding) clearConfirmation();

    window.addEventListener('pageshow', function (event) {
      // Restored from the back/forward cache: this page's Liquid is stale, so
      // `outstanding` cannot be trusted and the clear runs unconditionally.
      if (event.persisted) clearConfirmation();
    });
  })();
</script>
